There are countless waterfall options around Ubud and they're an excellent spot to refresh yourself after a hike under the sun. The time you go is always a key factor in relation to the number of tourists, but from my point of view, they're always enjoyable. That said: although they usually have maintenance and access stairs, keep in mind that after the rain there's often quite a bit of mud and slippery areas (not serious, just caution).

Although there are dozens of options, here are the three that we most highly recommend, as suggested by the locals we met along the way:

